 R←Test_API_040(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;msg2;buff;subject
⍝ Commits with a message that carries everything which used to be a problem: quotes of both
⍝ kinds, a backtick and a "$". The message used to travel on the command line, where it must be
⍝ enclosed by quotes, so <MassageMsg> replaced every quote in it by a backtick - and on Linux and
⍝ Mac OS the shell would have expanded "$HOME" and executed whatever sat between backticks. The
⍝ message now goes into a file which is passed with -F, so it arrives verbatim.\\
⍝ Both ways of committing are covered: with and without --amend.
⍝ Works on a private copy of the fixture because it commits.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 (⊂' r←Counter' ' r←4711')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/APLSource/Counter.aplf')1
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'add APLSource/Counter.aplf'

 msg←'He said "hi", it''s $HOME and a tick ` - 100% done'
 {}msg G.Commit tempDir
 (rc buff subject)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'log -1 --format=%s'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp msg≢⊃subject

 msg2←'Amended, and still with "quotes" and $PATH'
 {}msg2 G.Commit tempDir 1
 (rc buff subject)←tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'log -1 --format=%s'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠rc
 →T.GoToTidyUp msg2≢⊃subject

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
